A||||1||Mike Skora||Replacing shifter and cables
Z||000000||Mike Skora||07-22-99||11:29 AM||||I need to replace my shifter and both cables on my 86 GT.  Has anyone got any suggestions on how to begin such a project??<br>Thanks.
Z||000001||DJRice||07-22-99||02:56 PM||||Its not really that big of a deal.  You will need to remove the console and shifter cover/ashtray plate.  You will need to remove the ECM and its bracket.  After that, you just pull the pins and the retaining rings on the shifter, then undo the mounting bracket on the tranny and your done with the cables.<p>There are only 4 bolts holding the shifter itself in.  This one can get tricky.  If you dont mind taking the shifter handle loose from the entire asssembly, which is only one retaining ring, you will be able to pull the shifter assembly out from under the console carrier by only removing the rear screws that hold it in. (The console carrier is the long black *and fragile* plastic assembly that runs from the dash to the console)<p>Or you can pull your radio and ac controls, remove the bracket that holds them in, then remove all of the plastic clips on the carrier and carefully remove it to allow the shifter to come out in one piece.  <p>Installation is the reverse of removal.  (after reading that line in the haynes manual  100 times, ive always wanted an excuse to say it)
